  "body": "Closes #818\nClaim: cloud/i818b-sonnet\n\n### Problem\n\"[Topic Unique] Diablo IV\" is shown in full; legacy shows \"[TU] Diablo IV\".\n\n### Cause\nLOT-022 left `filterTU` out of the parser on purpose (D4, presentation concern) and no app lot picked it up.\n\n### Change\n- `HFRModels/Lists/TopicTitle.swift`: one pure `TopicTitle.displayed(_:)` (Foundation only), port of `filterTU` (`SuperHFRplus/Helpers/RangeOfCharacters.m:330-343` @ `87fe0d1c`): the 9 spellings, same order, case-insensitive literal match. Parsers keep the raw title.\n- Legacy call sites @ `87fe0d1c`: `Topic.m:90-94` (every topic title), `Classes/OfflineMessagesTableViewController.m:2348-2350` and `HFRswift/Wrapped/MessagesTableViewController.m:113-115` (reader title; the online reader inherits it). Note: the `OnlineMessagesTableViewController.m:2437` cited in #818 is a comment line at that revision, not the rule.\n- `TopicSummary.displayTitle` = `TopicTitle.displayed(title)`; views use it, no per-view copy.\n- App call sites (all that show a topic title):\n  - `Navigation/TopicRowView.swift`: forum lists, Favoris, search results (shared row)\n  - `Messages/MessageRowView.swift`: private-message list rows (legacy MP rows are `Topic`s too)\n  - `Navigation/MessagePlaceholderView.swift`: unreadable-link placeholder\n  - `Offline/OfflineTopicsView.swift`: offline list row\n  - `Reader/TopicReaderModel.swift` `title`: reader navigation title (page title and initial title; online and offline readers)\n  - `FilteredPosts/FilteredPostsModel.swift` `start(opening:)`: filtered-posts title\n- Not changed: the HTML `<title>` of the reader document (never displayed), titles sent back to HFR (raw).\n- Merged `dev-swift` (#921 moved the row markers to `Experimental/FlagIconRows/`; `TopicRowView` merged cleanly).\n\n### Tests\n`HFRModelsTests/TopicTitleTests.swift`: 9 spellings, case, position/several matches, literal dots of `T.U.`, no match (spacing kept), idempotence. With the rule disabled (`spellings.prefix(0)`) 15 issues fail; restored, they pass. SwiftLint `--strict` clean on the changed files. App code not built here (Linux).\n\nThe CI of the first draft failed on the draft-PR macOS gate and on the Docs consistency check (a `### Ledger` heading without a `ledger` label); no legacy gap row or changelog entry names `filterTU`, so this body has no ledger section.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CEn6UbP7MQZfLAuyub\n",
