   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, read-only sub-agent of cloud/orch; the author is Sonnet), head ccba38f0, verbatim:**\n\n> REQUEST CHANGES\n>\n> 1. Medium. `Packages/HFRKit/Tests/HFRParsingTests/TopicList/LegacyTitleRewrite.swift:5-17` (used in `TopicListDifferentialTests.swift:150` and `FavoritesParserTests.swift:59`). The PR adds a second copy of `filterTU` instead of reusing the existing test-only one. Issue #818's scope says to reuse it. As things stand, the oracle differential tests check the test copy, and the shipped `TopicTitle.displayed` is not tested against legacy output. If someone edits `TopicTitle.spellings` later, every differential test stays green. Fix: delete `LegacyTitleRewrite` and call `TopicTitle.displayed` in both tests. I tried this locally: all 26 tests in the differential, favourites and TopicTitle suites pass. Also update `docs/lots/LOT-022-topic-list-parser.md:15`, which still says \"not ported (… a test-only copy …)\" and is wrong once this PR lands (L08).\n>\n> Everything else checks out:\n> - The citations are correct at 87fe0d1c: `RangeOfCharacters.m:330-343`, `Topic.m:90-94`, `MessagesTableViewController.m:114` and `OfflineMessagesTableViewController.m:2349`. `OnlineMessagesTableViewController.m:2437` is only a comment.\n> - The nine spellings match legacy exactly, in the same order. The match is a case-insensitive literal, anywhere in the title, with no diacritic folding.\n> - The function is used for list, favourites, search and MP rows, and for the reader, filtered-posts and offline titles. Raw titles stay raw elsewhere.\n> - No deliberate gap, so no `### Ledger` section is needed.\n>\n> **Verified**\n> - `swift build --build-tests` and `swift test` (TopicTitleTests, differential, favourites) pass on Linux.\n> - Mutation check: dropping `.caseInsensitive` makes 3 of the 6 TopicTitle tests fail.\n> - `swiftlint lint --strict` on the 9 changed files: no violations.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
